From: corruptmods <13516012+corruptmods@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] vo_avfoundation: never wait on the main thread at teardown

preinit, uninit, recover_display_layer, ensure_osd_layer and
update_avfoundation_geometry (per frame with zoom or pan) did a
dispatch_sync to the main queue. uninit always did, to remove the layer's
KVO, so a host calling mpv_terminate_destroy() on its main thread
deadlocked: the core joins the VO thread, which waited for the main
thread. Any blocking libmpv call from the main thread could deadlock the
same way when it met vo_create()'s preinit rendezvous or a synchronous
VOCTRL.

The KVO observer becomes the VO's main-thread link (the "avf main-thread
link" region):

- uninit detaches the link under its lock (no main-thread wait) and hands
  the app-state observers, the KVO registration, the layers' timebase and
  the link's own references to a main-queue block. Callbacks reach the VO
  only through the link, so one that runs after uninit finds no VO. The
  timebase is cleared only if it is still this VO's.
- The main thread caches the layer's pixel size and gravity (from KVO, and
  from a coalesced refresh queued on every read); update_avfoundation_
  geometry reads the cache. A KVO change made off the main thread refreshes
  the cache on the main queue before it flags the VO.
- recover_display_layer reads the renderer's status and flushes on the VO
  thread, where the file already enqueues, flushes and reads status
  everywhere else.
- preinit's setup (timebase, observers, KVO, first geometry read) and the
  OSD layer's creation still wait for the main thread, at most 500 ms
  each, because the VO uses their results on its next frame. A block that
  runs later still completes, and sets pending_main_late; VOCTRL_CHECK_
  EVENTS then adopts the OSD layer and re-reads the geometry.

With a main thread that services its queue, the order and the values the
VO sees are what they were. Object lifetimes are unchanged except that the
last release of the observers, the display layer reference and the
timebase reference now happen on the main queue after uninit returns.

scripts/test_avf_main_thread_link.sh compiles the region against real
layers and the real main queue: teardown from a thread the main thread is
joining, a callback after detach, the geometry cache, the bounded wait
timing out and its late completion, and the OSD layer handoff.


